    "title": "Local Native American burial ground being restored by cemetery preservationists - NewsBreak",
    "text": "Beacon\nwebsite\nUpper Sandusky\nLocal Native American burial ground being restored by cemetery preservationists\n6 hours ago\nUPPER SANDUSKY – Tucked among trees on the edge of Harrison Smith Park in Upper Sandusky lies one of the most significant cemeteries in Ohio, the “Old Indian Burial Grounds.” Within the one-acre plot lies the graves of members of the Wyandotte Nation who lived on the land before white settlers arrived. It is estimated that between 60 and 100 people are buried there. Some are full-blooded Wyandottes, some are mixed blood, and some are white.",
